  "note": "Real per-player names and jersey numbers for the top 32 Belgian clubs, taken in pyramid order (groups N1A..N5A). The source lists players SURNAME-FIRST; the split below applies the Dutch/French particle rule (Van, Vande, De, Den, Der, du, le stay with the surname), so a few compound surnames such as 'Morel de Westgaver' may be split imperfectly - `nameRaw` preserves the original string in those cases. Per-player stats (points/goals/assists) exist on ultie.org but only on the tournament-wide statistics page, which is virtualised and renders ~12 rows at a time; they were not harvested. Team-level games/wins/losses are on each team page.",
  "excluded": "Four teams in the BUOC pyramid are not Belgian clubs and were skipped: Eulchtimate Open 1 and 2 (Lille, France), Ultimate Delux O (Luxembourg) and the U17 Open National Team.",
  "substitutions": "Five clubs registered near-empty rosters at the source (Mighty DUCs 2 players, Gentle Open Too 3, Les Hiboux Glorieux 3, Zero Gravity 4, Les Chouettes Glorieuses 4) and were replaced by fuller squads from the lower groups: Area 51 (21), Jetset Propellers (19), Frisco Duro (16), PUF (13) and Éclipse Lunaire (11). Each replacement carries `substitutedFor`. This deliberately breaks strict pyramid order - the replacements come from N5B/N6A/N6B - in exchange for usable squad sizes. Lievegem Frisbee Team was rejected as a candidate because half its roster is placeholder entries ('E E', 'F F', 'G G').",
  "dataQualityWarning": "Armada Open lists Kilian Walsh twice, both on #13 (the duplicate was dropped). Area 51 and Frisco Duro field women alongside men (flagged `mixedGenderSquad`) - Belgian Open is open in practice, same as Poland. Unlike the Polish file these were NOT filtered out; decide per your Open-division model.",
